# jeyanandan.com. A personal site: an introduction, the writing, and one
# outbound link to ko-fi.com. Nothing is embedded and nothing is submitted --
# every built page carries no <iframe>, no <form> and, today, no <script> at
# all. Fonts are the system's, there is no CDN and no analytics. img-src allows
# data: for the one-byte inline favicon in Base.astro.
#
# 2026-09-20, with the product pages: frame-src named ko-fi.com for a donation
# iframe that was replaced by a plain outbound link; form-action named ko-fi.com
# for a payment form that is not on the page; connect-src named
# api.formaddie.com and media-src allowed blob:/data: for the recorder, which is
# no longer built; and microphone=(self) was that recorder's microphone. All of
# them are gone. Verified against the built pages before the change: no iframe,
# frame, embed, object, form, formaction, script, fetch, XMLHttpRequest,
# WebSocket, getUserMedia, MediaRecorder, audio, video or blob: on any of /,
# /blog/, /blog/snowflake-fuckari-in-action/ or the 404.
#
# CACHING, 2026-09-20. HTML is never held by a shared cache without
# revalidation: a page removed from src/ has to stop being served promptly,
# and the home page's existing no-cache rule is the shape the rest of the site
# now follows. Assets split two ways. /_astro/* filenames carry Astro's
# content hash, so a change is a new URL and the old one can be immutable for
# a year. /figures/* filenames do NOT carry a hash -- fig-01..28 and the
# genealogy pair keep stable names and their contents do get corrected -- so
# they are long-lived at the edge (s-maxage, which a deploy purge flushes) and
# short in the browser (max-age + must-revalidate, which no purge can reach).
# Do not add immutable to /figures/*: a corrected diagram would then not reach
# a reader who had already loaded the old one.
#
# This file is NOT what served /privacy/, /important/, /auth-callback/ and
# /blog/neurodivergent/ as HTTP 200 after they were removed. Checked
# 2026-09-20: the Pages origin 404s all four (jeyanandan.pages.dev and a
# ?cb= query both 404 from the same deployment the apex serves), and no
# s-maxage=604800 or x-robots-tag string existed anywhere in this repo.
# Those four responses come from a cache at the jeyanandan.com zone, above
# the origin. Only a Cloudflare purge clears them; this file cannot.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; media-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/blog/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/figures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=604800, must-revalidate
